content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-109 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-23500; reported drive-end bearing-housing temperature 85 °C and vibration 2.5 mm/s.",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: the applicable manual limits are normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C, with bearing temperature measured on the housing surface. The reported 85 °C IR reading is therefore 15 °C above the normal maximum, 5 °C above the alarm limit and 5 °C below trip. It is an alarm condition, not a trip reading; SSP-07 requires a priority-1 work order within the shift. The evidence does not require an immediate stop solely for this temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: Figure 3 applies to vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. A reading of 2.5 mm/s is below the 2.8 mm/s RMS Zone A/B boundary and is therefore provisionally Zone A (0.0–2.8 mm/s RMS, labelled ‘New machines’), not the highest severity Zone D. This classification is conditional on confirming the RMS/housing measurement basis; both housings must be measured and the highest reading classified. The supplied reading does not trigger the Zone D immediate-stop rule.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage and no noise were reported; the evidence gives no numerical limits for these observations. The absence of seal leakage does not invoke the manual’s leakage-at-shaft-seal corrective action, while the absence of noise does not by itself exclude bearing wear or the other high-temperature causes.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing — listed first among the manual’s probable causes of high bearing temperature; check grease quantity before specifying any grease addition or removal.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear — also listed as a probable cause of high bearing temperature; inspect the bearings, and if replacement is required, renew both bearings as a pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment — also listed as a probable cause; check alignment and perform laser alignment after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Respond within the shift as P1. Verify the drive-end housing-surface temperature and measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings in mm/s RMS; classify the highest vibration reading using Figure 3. If the highest reading is in Zone D (7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS), stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Troubleshoot the high temperature by checking grease quantity, inspecting bearing condition and checking alignment. Complete non-intrusive checks first; defer intrusive inspection until the isolation controls in the next step are complete. Mechanical-seal replacement is not included in the base scope merely because of this report: no seal leakage was reported, and seal replacement is the manual’s corrective action for leakage at the shaft seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting. If removal of the back pull-out assembly is required, prepare its lift as a 68 kg lift using the signed lifting plan and certified-equipment controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After inspection, if the section 5.3 replacement condition is confirmed—wear, noise or high temperature in either bearing—or bearing replacement is otherwise authorised, replace both bearings as a pair: one HF3-512 drive-end bearing 6312-C3 and one HF3-510 non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Do not replace only one bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, tighten any disturbed M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm with lightly oiled threads. If the casing is opened, fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket and tighten M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm with lightly oiled threads; do not assume casing opening is necessary for back pull-out work.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, use a laser alignment tool. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before returning the pump to operation, ensure the Plan 11 seal flush is from pump discharge and never run the seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Stage one conditionally for an authorised bearing-pair replacement; install together with HF3-510 rather than replacing this bearing alone.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Stage one conditionally for an authorised bearing-pair replacement; install together with HF3-512.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, required only if the casing is opened. Back pull-out construction permits rotating-assembly removal without disturbing the casing or pipework, so consumption is not assumed for the base inspection scope.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal: electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves; and a line-break permit, with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg and requires lifting equipment. Because it exceeds the site’s 25 kg threshold, any lift of this assembly requires a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the pump is on a chemically dosed line, chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory; the line’s chemical-dosing status must be confirmed before deciding whether this control applies.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current supplied vibration reading does not invoke the immediate-stop rule. If subsequent measurement of either housing places the highest reading in Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair, only if inspection authorises replacement: standard time 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard time 1.5 hours with 1 technician; required after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450 and Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, but Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, applies to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. Serial HF3-23500 is within that range, so the bulletin governs any seal work on this asset: do not fit HF3-450; use the pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, with no sleeve measurement needed for seal setting, and tighten its gland nuts to 30 Nm rather than 25 Nm. This applicability decision does not itself authorise seal replacement in the current no-leakage scope.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 2.5 mm/s vibration an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and what is the vibration reading on the other housing? Both housings must be measured and the highest reading classified before the zone assessment is final (C06, C07).",
    "Has bearing wear, noise or bearing high temperature been confirmed sufficiently to authorise bearing-pair replacement? The report establishes a housing-temperature alarm, but the troubleshooting table also requires checks for over-greasing and misalignment; no confirmed parts consumption is assumed (C09, C10).",
    "What is the specified correct grease quantity, and what grease correction, if any, is required? The evidence says to check grease quantity but supplies no target quantity or grease specification (C09).",
    "Will the authorised repair require removal/lifting of the 68 kg back pull-out assembly or opening of the casing? These determine whether the lifting-plan and casing-gasket contingencies become mandatory; the supplied bearing-replacement extract does not give a step-by-step disassembly procedure (C01, C02, C05, C10).",
    "Is P-109 installed on a chemically dosed line? This determines whether chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required (C15).",
    "What operating restriction or monitoring, if any, should apply while awaiting P1 attendance? The evidence gives the alarm response and a 90 °C trip value but no specific continued-operation instructions for the 80–90 °C interval (C02, C15).",
    "Table 6 gives no standard labour time for diagnosis, grease correction or bearing inspection; those durations cannot be estimated from the supplied evidence (C12)."
  ]
}
